<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_Warcasket_Siegebreaker (VFEPirates.WarcasketDef,
    ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase") at VFEP commit e237aba (2026-08-29),
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml. Everything not listed under
    "Tuning" below is still a verbatim Siegebreaker copy (placeholder, per
    TODOs.md), the VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets research prereq included.

    Tuning (2026-09-13, retuned 2026-09-17). VFEP reference numbers are the
    10th-generation sets (Siegebreaker, Guardian, Controller, Sarcophagus, Brute)
    at the commit above. The set is a close-combat suit and is pitched at Brute and
    Guardian effectiveness, priced a little under them:
    - ArmorRating_Blunt 1.5 (Brute and Guardian; the other three 1.0): the
      close-combat plating, carried by all three pieces so the set reads as one
      tier, the Guardian pattern. Sharp 2 and Heat 1 are the shared spacer values.
    - EnergyShieldEnergyMax 2.5 (Siegebreaker 2.5; Guardian, Controller and
      Sarcophagus 1.5; Brute 5.0). The bubble blocks ranged fire only, which is
      exactly what a melee suit needs while closing, so the 09-13 value of 2.0 was
      undercutting the set's own role. EnergyShieldRechargeRate stays at the
      shared 0.01.
    - costList ComponentSpacer 6 / Plasteel 180 / Uranium 50 (Siegebreaker
      6 / 145 / 50, Guardian 6 / 200 / 50). VFEP uses the spacer-component count
      as a tech-complexity dial (Controller 12 for mech control, the utility sets
      6, Brute 4); a fuel-burning drop thruster is Aerial-tier tech, so the
      09-13 count of 8 came back down to 6 and the plating step went onto
      plasteel instead. At vanilla market values (plasteel 9, spacer component
      200, uranium 6) the full set welds for about 4690 silver without Odyssey:
      Siegebreaker 4195, Sarcophagus 4785, Guardian 5164, Brute 5220. The
      shoulders and helmet scale with the armor at the ratios the 10th-gen sets
      use between their pieces; see their headers for the arithmetic.

    SOS2/Universum parity: VFEP's 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml matches its own
    warcasket armor/helmet defs by an explicit defName list, so it never reaches
    this mod's defs. Our 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml applies the same EVA tag and
    Insulation_Cold override to this def and the helmet; see its header.

    Vanilla Gravship Expanded parity: VGE1's ArmorVacuumResistancePatch.xml
    lowers the five VFEP spacer warcasket armors to VacuumResistance 0.22 (helmets
    0.65) by defName, so a full set needs an oxygen source; it never reaches this
    def. Our 1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/VacuumResistance.xml
    (gated on VGE1's package id in LoadFolders.xml) applies the same 0.22 here;
    see its header. Without VGE1 the 0.2 below stands.

    Abilities (2026-09-16, design approved that day): the armor is the drop engine.
    - Breach Jump: VEF CompAbilitiesApparel grants SCWC_BreachJump (rules and numbers
      in 1.6/Defs/AbilityDefs/BreachJump.xml and Source/1.6/Abilities/), fuelled by
      the CompApparelReloadable beside it (100 charges of chemfuel at 1 per charge,
      60-tick reload, 20 per jump; Aerial's tank). The ability reads the tank off
      the apparel that holds it, so both comps must sit on this one def, which is
      why the engine is here and not on the shoulders as on Aerial.
    - SCWC_BreachJumpRange +20: the set's whole planet-side range (the shoulders
      and helmet add none; Aerial's full set reaches 40). In space the jump has no
      range limit and requires line of sight instead.
    - Space walking and the astrofuel swap under Vanilla Gravship Expanded come
      from 1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/; stock Odyssey space terrain
      is impassable, so the main tree carries neither.
    - costList GravlitePanel 30 under Odyssey (MayRequire on the cost item, as
      Core's Buildings_Exotic.xml does for ShuttleEngine): the drop thrusters are
      gravtech. The shoulders take 10 and the helmet 10 (the VGE2 combat vacsuit's
      20 / 10 split was the 09-16 starting point; the armor rose to 30 on 09-17
      because the thrusters and the unlimited-range space flight are its). A panel
      is market value 4 but costs 1 plasteel, 5 vacstone blocks and 1800 work
      (Odyssey's Items_Resource_Misc.xml), and vacstone only comes from space, so
      the 50-panel set total is the Odyssey premium: a been-to-orbit gate rather
      than a silver one, which is why the extra space functionality is priced
      here and not in the base costList.

    Not carried over from VFEP, on purpose: VFEP's 1.6/Patches/Odyssey.xml does
    not touch any warcasket apparel def by defName. It only adds a PawnKindDef
    (VFEP_Salvager_Warcasket) whose apparelTags/weaponTags include
    WarcasketVeteran, so it is not itself a reason to gate anything here on
    Odyssey.

    apparel tags: checked 1.6/Defs/PawnKindDefs_Humanlikes/PawnKinds_Mercenaries.xml,
    PawnKinds_Junkers.xml and 1.6/Patches/Odyssey.xml for both tags.
    - WarcasketVeteran is used by VFEP_Major (Mercenaries) and VFEP_Veteran
      (Junkers) apparelTags/weaponTags, plus Odyssey's VFEP_Salvager_Warcasket
      apparelTags/weaponTags: every veteran-tier raid pawnkind across both
      factions, not just Odyssey content. Left commented out below per
      TODOs.md's open question (reusing it puts this set on all of them).
    - WarcasketAll is used only by VFEP_General (Mercenaries), the faction
      leader pawnkind. Included below.
    Art: Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcracker
    (+ _north/_east/_south), 256x256 RGBA under the root Textures/ folder, mirroring
    VFEP's own warcasket layout.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker</defName>
    <label>shipcracker warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Placeholder shipcracker warcasket shell. Stats are an untuned copy of the siegebreaker warcasket for now.</shortDescription>
    <description>Placeholder description for the shipcracker warcasket shell. It is a stand-in for later tuning, not lore.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcracker</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>50</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>80</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>80</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
      <EnergyShieldRechargeRate>0.01</EnergyShieldRechargeRate>
      <EnergyShieldEnergyMax>2.5</EnergyShieldEnergyMax>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.2</VacuumResistance>
      <SCWC_BreachJumpRange>20</SCWC_BreachJumpRange>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>6</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>180</Plasteel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
      <GravlitePanel MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">30</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcracker</wornGraphicPath>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <!-- Reusing WarcasketVeteran puts this set on every Junker/Mercenary
             veteran-tier pawnkind (and Odyssey's salvager pawnkind); see
             TODOs.md open question.
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        -->
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_ApparelReloadable">
        <maxCharges>100</maxCharges>
        <ammoDef>Chemfuel</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <hotKey>Misc4</hotKey>
        <chargeNoun>fuel</chargeNoun>
        <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>SCWC_BreachJump</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.CompProperties_ShieldBubble">
        <compClass>VEF.Apparels.CompShieldBubble</compClass>
        <blockRangedAttack>true</blockRangedAttack>
        <blockMeleeAttack>false</blockMeleeAttack>
        <showWhenDrafted>true</showWhenDrafted>
        <showOnHostiles>true</showOnHostiles>
        <showOnNeutralInCombat>true</showOnNeutralInCombat>
        <shieldTexPath>Other/ShieldBubble</shieldTexPath>
        <chargeFullyWhenMade>true</chargeFullyWhenMade>
        <minShieldSize>2.1</minShieldSize>
        <maxShieldSize>2.7</maxShieldSize>
        <disableRotation>true</disableRotation>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>VFEP_WarcasketTrait</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
